# Project Rules
- Framework: Next.js (App Router) with TypeScript
- Styling: Tailwind CSS
- Path alias: `@/*` maps to `./*` (root-level imports, no `src/` directory)
- Components are organized by page under `components/stock/<page>/` (the tab component + its sub-components). Shared shell in `components/layout/`; shared primitives in `components/shared/`; planned-page stubs in `components/planned/`.
- No database/ORM (no Prisma); no persistence layer yet
- No Server Actions directory
- Strict TypeScript types; no Zod used currently

## lib/ folder structure (numbered by call-stack order, entry → fallback)
```
lib/
├── 0.entry/          get-stock-data.ts      — entry point, called first by API route
├── 1.api/            yahoo-api.ts           — fetches raw Yahoo data (1st real call)
├── 2.data/           dividend.ts            — page converters (called by entry)
│   ├── financials.ts
│   ├── overview.ts
│   ├── profitability.ts
│   └── sensitivity.ts
├── 3.tools/          fundamentals-tools.ts  — reusable converters (called by data)
│   └── market-tools.ts
├── 4.screening/      screening.ts           — business rules (called by data)
├── 5.utils/          utils.ts               — helpers (called by data & screening)
├── 6.types/          types.ts               — TypeScript interfaces (StockData, FiscalPeriod, etc.)
└── 7.mock/           mock-data.ts           — fallback data (used on error)
```

## Data flow (call order)
API route (`app/api/stock/[symbol]/route.ts`)
→ `0.entry/get-stock-data.ts` (`getStockData`)
→ `1.api/yahoo-api.ts` (`fetchRawStockData`)
→ `2.data/*.ts` (5 page converters, each owns a slice of `StockData`)
→ `3.tools/*` (`FundamentalsTools`, `MarketTools`) and `4.screening/screening.ts`
→ `5.utils/utils.ts` (formatters, CAGR, `isMissing`, `closestPrice`)
→ `7.mock/mock-data.ts` (fallback only on error)

## Key dependencies
- `yahoo-finance2` — Yahoo Finance data fetching
- `recharts` — charting
- `lucide-react` — icons
- `clsx` + `tailwind-merge` — className utilities (`cn()` helper in utils)
- `tsx` — test runner

## Test command
`npm run test:data` — runs `scripts/test-calculators.ts` (offline, Yahoo-shaped fixtures, no network)

## Conventions
- `isMissing()` treats null/undefined/NaN as "no value" (JSON.stringify converts NaN→null)
- "N-year figure" = N data points (5yr CAGR needs 5 points, growthYears=4)
- Fiscal years may not end Dec 31; real period-end dates are preserved
- Current/incomplete calendar year is excluded from annual data
- Yahoo reports capex/dividends/buybacks as negatives; tools convert to positive
- `FundamentalsTools.annualPeriods()` is memoized per request via WeakMap

## Living document rule
- Every time you learn something new about this project (a new convention, dependency, file responsibility, quirk, or pattern), add it to this `.clinerules` file so future sessions don't re-learn it.
